{"name":"Limelight","hex":"#eee96b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"limelight","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The intense white light produced when heating lime in an oxyhydrogen flame.","A type of stage lighting once used in theatres and music halls, producing a bright light by the use of incandescent quicklime."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["to illuminate with limelight"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/limelight"}],"entries":[{"title":"Limelight","blocks":[{"text":"Limelight  is a non-electric type of stage lighting that was once used in theatres and music halls. An intense illumination is created when a flame fed by oxygen and hydrogen is directed at a cylinder of quicklime, due to a combination of incandescence and candoluminescence."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Limelight_diagram.svg/330px-Limelight_diagram.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Limelight","wikidata":"Q555987"},{"title":"Limelight (1952 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Limelight is a 1952 American comedy-drama film written, produced, directed by, and starring Charlie Chaplin, based on a novella by Chaplin titled Footlights. The score was composed by Chaplin and arranged by Ray Rasch."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Limelight_%281952%29_-_original_theatrical_poster.jpeg/330px-Limelight_%281952%29_-_original_theatrical_poster.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Limelight_(1952_film)","wikidata":"Q584509"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Homemade_Limelight.JPG/500px-Homemade_Limelight.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Homemade_Limelight.JPG/1280px-Homemade_Limelight.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Homemade_Limelight.JPG/500px-Homemade_Limelight.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Heating calcium hydroxide (slaked lime) in a stove burner causes it to glow, although this is not as bright as a real limelight.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHomemade_Limelight.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Limelight_%2819e_eeuw%29.jpg/500px-Limelight_%2819e_eeuw%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Limelight_%2819e_eeuw%29.jpg/1280px-Limelight_%2819e_eeuw%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Limelight_%2819e_eeuw%29.jpg/500px-Limelight_%2819e_eeuw%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A 19th century limelight used for stage lighting. Collection: Stadsschouwburg (city theatre) Bruges, Belgium.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALimelight_(19e_eeuw).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Limelight_promo_crop.jpg/330px-Limelight_promo_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Limelight_promo_crop.jpg/330px-Limelight_promo_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Limelight (1952) was a serious and autobiographical film for Chaplin. His character, Calvero, is an ex–music hall star (described in this image as a \"Tramp Comedian\") forced to deal with his loss of popularity.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALimelight_promo_crop.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Chaplin_-_Bloom_-_1952-1.jpg/500px-Chaplin_-_Bloom_-_1952-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Chaplin_-_Bloom_-_1952-1.jpg/500px-Chaplin_-_Bloom_-_1952-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Charlie Chaplin and Claire Bloom in Limelight ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChaplin_-_Bloom_-_1952-1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/3e/The_terry_theme_-_charles_chaplin_-_bourne_inc.jpg/250px-The_terry_theme_-_charles_chaplin_-_bourne_inc.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3e/The_terry_theme_-_charles_chaplin_-_bourne_inc.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/3e/The_terry_theme_-_charles_chaplin_-_bourne_inc.jpg/250px-The_terry_theme_-_charles_chaplin_-_bourne_inc.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sheet music cover of \"The Terry Theme\", by Charlie Chaplin, and published by Bourne, Inc.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_terry_theme_-_charles_chaplin_-_bourne_inc.jpg"}],"sounds":{"limelight":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/ff/En-us-limelight.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/f/ff/En-us-limelight.ogg/En-us-limelight.ogg.mp3"}]}}}